questions.passage_md:
A mall charges ₹20 an hour for cars and ₹10 an hour for bikes; any part of an hour counts as a full hour, and every hour after the third costs double. Its program uses two functions:

```python
import math

def hours_charged(minutes):
    return math.ceil(minutes / 60)

def fee(minutes, vehicle="car"):
    rate = 20 if vehicle == "car" else 10
    h = hours_charged(minutes)
    if h > 3:
        return 3 * rate + (h - 3) * rate * 2
    return h * rate

print(fee(50), fee(130, "bike"), fee(250))
```
